### 2026-08-30 — `create_figures.ipynb`: Fig 2 → 2×3 in Fig 1's exact format, split by fitting variant
- **User directive (final of two same-session passes):** compare **weighted
  test-set metrics to unweighted full-population metrics** (`gap = weighted test
  − unweighted population`) — the fixed quantity — "using both weighted and
  unweighted models," in a **format similar to Figure 1**. Purpose: does the
  weighted test-set estimate match what would happen in the population?
- **Two attempts this pass; the second is what shipped.** First reshaped 1×3 →
  2×3 with **rows = test-metric evaluation weighting** (unweighted-eval top,
  weighted-eval bottom) and grouped grey/accent bars per panel — misread
  "unweighted/weighted models" as the evaluation weighting. User clarified the
  gap is fixed (weighted test − unweighted population) and the split is by
  **model** (fitting variant). **Final cell `543d79e8` is 2×3 in Fig 1's exact
  format:** columns = models, **top row = unweighted (standard) model, all GREY;
  bottom row = survey-weighted model, all ACCENT**, one single-color horizontal
  bar per metric (no grouped bars, no per-panel legend). `test_df` filtered back
  to `weighting == "weighted"`; `gen_df` = pop/test merge, `gap = test −
  population`; row loop over `row_variants = [("standard","Unweighted\\nmodel",
  GREY), ("survey_weighted","Survey-weighted\\nmodel", ACCENT)]` with rotated
  left-column annotate labels. X-label "Weighted test-split score − unweighted
  population score (nearer 0 = better estimate)" on bottom-row middle; suptitle
  "Weighted test estimate vs. population performance (mean over {N_ITER}
  iterations)". Symmetric shared x-axis `±|gap|.max()×1.45` (≈±0.005) so the
  tiny gaps are legible.
- **Finding:** all gaps ~+0.000 to +0.004 → the weighted test set is a
  near-unbiased estimate of population performance for both model types. Largest
  is NN standard recall (+0.004); a few survey-weighted precision/f1/recall gaps
  go slightly negative (XGB). ROC-AUC is the one the survey-weighted model
  estimates *high* (+0.001–0.002).
- **Note:** this is the same gap the 2026-08-30 1×3 entry (below) plotted, now
  just laid out as two single-color rows (fitting variant) instead of one panel
  with grouped bars — a pure presentation change to match Fig 1.
- **Durability:** single atomic `json.dump` write, `._*` swept first, `sync` +
  re-read confirmed the 13-cell state stuck and the cell is 2-row / weighted-
  filtered / `row_variants`-based (no `row_weightings` leftover). **Verified
