### 2026-08-11 — NN topped up to 20 genuine iterations; `create_figures.ipynb` averages over iterations
- **Context:** the NN had 15 iterations (iter0–14) plus a second `--iterations 5`
  batch that logged under `{variant}_iter{0..4}_*` and reproduced iter0–4
  **byte-identically** — the driver restarts the per-iteration seed at `SEED+0..4`
  each invocation (`SEED + it`, `it` = loop index from 0), so a plain re-run
  replays the same draws. Those batch-2 runs were briefly renamed iter15→19
  (parquets copied) to fake "20 iterations", but that just duplicated iter0–4
  with zero added variance. **Resolution: delete the fakes, add a temporary
  continuation flag, run the real iter15–19, then remove the flag.**
- **Deleted the 180 duplicate runs** (`_iter1[5-9]_*`) via `MlflowClient.delete_run`
  and `rm`'d the copied `..._iter{15..19}.parquet`, returning NN to 15 genuine
  iterations first.
- **`neural_network.py`: added, used, then removed a `--start-iteration` flag.**
  Temporarily changed the loop to
  `range(args.start_iteration, args.start_iteration + args.iterations)` so `it`
  (which drives the sample seed `SEED + it`, the split `random_state`, the run
  names, and the parquet filename) could continue past 14. Ran it in two pieces:
  a first `--start-iteration 15 --iterations 5` background job was **killed** at
  ~3.5/5 iterations (iter15–17 complete, iter18 half-done — one population run
  missing, iter19 not started); cleaned iter18's 35 partial runs + parquet and
  finished with `--start-iteration 18 --iterations 2` (exit 0). Final NN state:
  **20 distinct iterations (0–19), no duplicate names, iter15–19 on seeds 57–61
  and genuinely independent** (e.g. iter18 test ROC-AUC 0.6645 ≠ iter3 0.6647).
  Per user directive the flag was then **removed** — loop, argparse arg, and
  docstring reverted to the original single-`range(args.iterations)` form
  (`py_compile` clean, no `start-iteration` string remains). NB: the driver is
  once again replay-on-rerun; if a future top-up is needed, re-add the one-liner
  from this entry (git history has it). LR/XGB share the identical `SEED + it`
  pattern and would need the same.
- **`create_figures.ipynb` setup cell** rewritten for the iteration average:
  - MLflow metric query dedups by `(model, variant, iteration)` — `TEST_RE`
    gained an iteration capture group; a `best` dict keeps the latest run per
    iteration. Defensive against a continuation run re-logging an existing
    iteration name; a no-op now that indices are unique.
  - `N_ITER` is a per-model-aware string (`n_iter_by_model` counts distinct
    iterations, collapsing to one number when the models agree else a range) —
    now **"20"** for all three, so the three suptitles read "over 20 iterations".
    Dropped the unused `from collections import Counter`.
- **Validated** in a standalone script against the real store: MLflow →
  {LR:20, XGB:20, NN:20}, parquet globs → {20,20,20}, `N_ITER="20"`, iter18/19
  independent of iter3/4. **Not** rendered in Jupyter (standing "don't run
  headless" preference) — open and run all cells to eyeball layout.

### 2026-08-07 — `create_figures.ipynb`: average metrics over iterations, drop calibration
- **User directive:** make the metrics figures display the average over the
  iterations that were run, and remove the calibration plot.
- **Setup cell rewritten for the iteration architecture.** Was filtering
  `attributes.run_name = '{variant}_test'` and taking the single best run by
  `test_weighted_roc_auc`. Now regex-matches every `{variant}_iter{N}_test`
  run (`^(standard|survey_weighted)_iter\d+_test$`), collects all `test_*`
  metrics, and **means them per (model, variant, weighting, metric)** into
  `metrics_df`. Added `N_ITER` (max test-run count per model/variant, = 20
  here) for figure titles. Verified against the manual summary stats: the
  averaged LR values match exactly (e.g. standard unweighted ROC-AUC 0.6644,
  precision 0.2051; 40 test runs → 400 metric rows → mean over 20 iters).
- **Robust to partial runs.** `MODELS` is now filtered to models whose MLflow
  experiment exists (`get_experiment_by_name is not None`), so the notebook
  runs with only LR present (XGB/NN never ran — no experiments, no labeled
  parquets). Fig 1 grid and the confusion grid size to `len(MODEL_ORDER)` with
  `squeeze=False`, so 1 model doesn't leave empty panels or break `axes[i,j]`
  indexing (`subplots(1,2)` would otherwise return a 1-D array).
- **Labeled-parquet loading repointed to per-iteration glob + concat.** Was
  reading a single `data/test_labeled_<model>.parquet`; now globs
  `data/test_labeled_<model>_iter*.parquet` and `pl.concat`s all 20 (→ 1M
  pooled rows for LR). Confusion matrices (Fig 3) pool cleanly over that.
- **Figure 2 lost its population-weighted panel (user-approved).** The new 50k
  labeled parquets are 5-col (`TARGET` + proba/binary per variant) — **no
  `State population` column**, and the rows are a shuffled subset that no
  longer row-aligns to `data/test.parquet`, so the old `pred * state_pop`
  population-weighted rate is unrecoverable without changing the drivers to
  persist a weight column + re-running. Asked; user chose **drop the panel**.
  Fig 2 is now a single-panel unweighted predicted-positive-rate vs actual,
  pooled over iterations. (If both panels are wanted back, persist `State
  population` into the labeled parquet in the drivers and re-run — then restore
  the 1×2 layout.)
- **Calibration removed.** Deleted the `## Figure 4` markdown cell and the
  `calibration_curve` / ECE code cell entirely (per the drop request; this
  also sheds the only dependency on the `predicted_proba_*` columns for a
  figure, though those columns are still present in the parquets).
- **Not rendered in Jupyter.** Per the standing "don't run this headless"
  preference, only the data cells (MLflow query + averaging + parquet pooling)
  were validated in a standalone script; open the notebook and run all cells
  to eyeball layout (empty-panel sizing at 1 model, single-panel Fig 2,
  pooled confusion percentages).

